//! Store ↔ CAS composition module — GENERATED by `ggen sync run` from the
//! `strata-store-pack` ontology (https://strata.chatman.ai/ontology#).
//! Do not edit by hand.
//!
//! COMPOSITION LAW (derived, 2026-10-13): the store's content-address law
//! is key = SHA-256(value) at KEY_LEN = 32 bytes, and the pack's
//! content-address KAT folds three witnessed payloads under
//! InMemoryStore::root_digest — SHA-256 over the concatenated 32-byte keys
//! in BTreeMap lexicographic byte order — to the pinned root
//! a8378cfa.... A root over concatenated 32-byte digests is structurally a
//! CAS MerkleCommit root (st:merkleRoot = SHA-256(st:canonicalPayload);
//! the concatenated keys ARE the canonical payload), so every store key is
//! a valid CAS content address under the shared digest-shape law
//! ^[0-9a-f]{64}$, and this module admits the pinned KAT root as a CAS
//! content-address witness. Gate: gates/030_store_cas_composition.rq
//! (fail-closed). The strata-cas-pack graph is not imported: the
//! composition is pinned by literal — the same literals verify.py
//! recomputes.
